<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n86911" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προ-γνωστικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>foreknowing, prescient,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δύναμις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ph.
					1.659
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				2.164
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μόριον . . τῆς ψυχῆς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.433a
				</span></i>
			; of persons, <i><span class="en">
				M.Ant.
				8.25
			</span></i>; esp. of astrologers, <i><span class="en">
				Vett.Val.
				37.28
			</span></i>, al.: c. gen., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. τῆς κινήσεως τῶν νοσημάτων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Gal.
					17(1).243
				</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ π.</span>”
				<i>a sign of the future, prognostic,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Gp.
					1.2
				</span></i>
			 tit.: <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προγνωστικόν, τό,</span> name of a treatise by <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
			</span></i>; also title of work by Epicurus, <i><span class="en">
				D.L.
				10.28
			</span></i>; but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κή, ἡ,</span> name of an antidote, <i><span class="en">
				Damocr.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				14.134
			</span></i>. Adv.<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κῶς</span>
			<u>Gloss.</u>
        </div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
